abstract: >-
  Modern dataset prepared by poplolioi11 / 一卦 yigua.art from the Princeton
  Theological Seminary Library witness digitized by Internet Archive as
  sacredbooksofchi16conf. Historical English translator: James Legge (1882).
  Includes 64 judgments, 384 line passages and two additional paragraphs from
  printed pages 57–210, not the complete book. The source layer records selected
  upstream OCR; the reader layer normalizes typography and documents targeted
  corrections. Existing judgment strings retain their separate dated source audit
  and unrecorded original ingestion. This is an OCR-assisted initial transcription
  with targeted AI scan checks on 29 page images, without full-image proofreading
  or independent human second collation. All 450 reader strings are unchanged
  from the 0.1.0 website snapshot. Published on 23 October 2026; the version and
  concept DOIs are registered as findable. Archived files retain their historical
  preparation-state statements; this main-branch citation is a post-publication
  update and does not replace archived files. Public-domain historical text has no
  new CC restrictions; CC BY 4.0 applies only to copyrightable original modern
  metadata, documentation and arrangement. Images and private processing tools
  are not redistributed.
keywords:
  - Yî King
  - I Ching
  - James Legge
  - "1882"
  - OCR-assisted initial transcription
  - digital humanities
  - TEI
